summary: 'Builder shipped Wave 2 cleanly with one prerequisite pull-forward: registered the hidden `internal` command group + `active-remediations` subcommand in paradigm/src/index.ts (was Wave 3 territory but blocking Wave 2''s bash invocation). Then added _REMEDIATIONS_JSON cache (lines 87-94) and Check 14 (lines 908-960) to paradigm-common.sh. Critical placement decision: Check 14 placed BEFORE _compliance_snapshot at line 962 so guard violations roll into the snapshot''s VIOLATION_COUNT — preserves Loid data continuity for absent-Rune learning. Mirrors regenerated to all three locations. Build clean, 320 tests pass / 1 skip (no regression). Manual smoke test verified field extraction (id, severity, claimant, reason) + comma-bounded id matching for PARADIGM_OVERRIDE.'
