learnings:
  - Wave 3 prerequisite (registering hidden internal command) was load-bearing for Wave 2 — bash hook can't shell out to a command that doesn't exist. Builder did the right thing pulling it forward rather than blocking on it.
  - Check 14 placement BEFORE _compliance_snapshot is the right pattern — guard violations need to increment VIOLATION_COUNT before snapshot serialization so absent-Rune Loid sees the right data continuity.
  - 'Bash field extraction via grep+sed against producer-controlled JSON works for shape-stable data — no jq dependency needed for the simple case. Tradeoff: brittle if helper output shape changes.'
